# BEACON Phase 3 — .gitignore
# Strategy (current): CANONICAL GABBE LAYOUT (matches Super-Brand / kaiban-distributed).
# The GABBE kit + agent wiring + manifest (agents/, .claude/, .gabbe/) are LOCAL-ONLY — present on
# disk and fully USED at runtime by the agent (governance, skills, memory, checkpoints), but NOT
# committed (keeps the repo lean; the kit is regenerable from /home/andrei/work/AI/GABBE).
# COMMITTED project work: audit/, docs/ (discovery, requirements, architecture incl. ADRs, api),
# schemas/, gabbe.config.json, .mcp.json, .env.example, README. IGNORE caches/runtime/build/secrets.

# ── Secrets / env ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Belt-and-suspenders: ignore every .env variant except the committed example.
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── GABBE kit / wiring / manifest: LOCAL-ONLY (used at runtime, not committed) ─
# agents/ holds AGENTS.md, CONSTITUTION.md, skills, guides, templates, personas, and the live
# memory subsystem (PROJECT_STATE, SDLC_TRACKER, RESUME_POINTER, CONTINUITY, AUDIT_LOG, episodic
# snapshots, semantic knowledge). These persist on disk and any agent resumes from them losslessly;
# they are simply not version-controlled (canonical GABBE layout). The durable record of decisions
# also lives in committed docs/ (ADRs, SPEC) so nothing critical is lost from git history.
agents
.claude
.gabbe
project/state.db
project/logs/
project/runs/
*.gabbe-bak
*.gabbe-bak/

# ── Python tooling caches (if the optional gabbe CLI is run locally) ─────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
gabbe.egg-info/

# ── Node / Next.js build output (appears at S05+) ────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
coverage/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Playwright ephemeral run output (keep the committed visual baselines under e2e/*-snapshots/) ──
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# ── Editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tmp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── Internal contest-strategy docs (for our eyes only — never published; D-31) ──
docs/audit/RUBRIC_DEFENSIBILITY.md
docs/audit/JUDGE_SCORE_PREDICTION.md
docs/audit/PORTAL_ENTRY_VERIFICATION.md

# ── Entrant-only submission material — LOCAL ONLY, NEVER committed, NEVER exported ──
# Owner decision 2026-09-11. These are working documents for the entrant, not product docs:
#   • SUBMISSION_PACKAGE.md holds three Google Drive `?usp=sharing` links — two videos and a full
#     archive of the codebase. Anyone holding such a link can open the file without permission, so a
#     repository that carried them would hand out the archive the moment it went public.
#   • SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md and MASTER_PLAN.md are entrant process and per-criterion planning.
# They stay on disk so the owner can use them; git must never see them again.
#
# NOTE, and it matters: untracking a file does NOT remove it from git HISTORY. These three remain in
# earlier commits of THIS repository, which is private and stays private. The public repository
# (QUEST-BEACON) is built by export and has never contained them — verified 2026-09-11.
MASTER_PLAN.md
docs/SUBMISSION_PACKAGE.md
docs/SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md

# Next.js generated
next-env.d.ts
.next/types/

# Drizzle generated migrations dir (regenerated)
# drizzle/   # (keep committed once real migrations exist)

# Kubernetes: filled secret manifests never leave the machine
infra/k8s/*secrets.yaml
!infra/k8s/*secrets.example.yaml
public/maplibre/
